# Everything a RUNNING stack creates in its own directory. None of these is tracked today; listing
# them makes that deliberate rather than lucky — this directory is both the source tree and, once
# copied to a server, a live stack dir, so a careless `git add -A` in the wrong copy would otherwise
# commit an agent's overlay or a deploy key.
#
# The real files are made from the *.example ones beside them (mounts, port-forwards, service-env,
# hub-services/, compose.project.yml) or generated on the host (compose.override.yml, by
# gen-hub-mounts.sh), or templated onto the server by a config-management tool.

# --- live stack state (bind mounts) ---
data/                 # repo, goldens, per-box upper layers, the shared claude config, pinchtab
db-init/              # project seed data
git-identity/         # the hub's GitHub deploy key + gitconfig — NEVER commit
boxes/

# --- per-stack config made from the .example files (holds credentials) ---
.env
service-env
box-env
mounts
port-forwards
hub-services/
compose.project.yml
# Rendered from `mounts` by gen-hub-mounts.sh, on the host it runs on.
compose.override.yml

# --- python bytecode from the test suite's stub broker ---
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# --- the project's own build toolchain (made from build-setup.sh.example) ---
build-setup.sh
